---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const structuredData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Article",
	headline: "EkNepal: A First Attempt at Building Around Uncertainty",
	description:
		"A project note on EkNepal, a news-aggregation product that brings reporting from multiple Nepali publications into one interface, and my work as a frontend contributor through Alpinist Studios.",
	image: "https://atishaya7777.github.io/assets/eknepal/eknepal-fig-1-homepage.jpg",
	author: {
		"@type": "Person",
		name: "Atishaya Maharjan",
		url: "https://atishaya7777.github.io",
	},
	about: {
		"@type": "WebApplication",
		name: "EkNepal",
		url: "https://eknepal.com/",
		applicationCategory: "News aggregator",
	},
};
---

<Layout
	title="EkNepal — A First Attempt at Building Around Uncertainty · Atishaya Maharjan"
	description="Project note on EkNepal, a news-aggregation platform bringing reporting from multiple Nepali publications into one interface. My first paid programming project — a frontend contribution through Alpinist Studios."
	image="/assets/eknepal/eknepal-fig-1-homepage.jpg"
	imageAlt="Screenshot of EkNepal's news interface, showing a top-stories carousel and articles attributed to their source publications"
	type="article"
	structuredData={structuredData}
>
	<article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">

		<!-- ── Title block ── -->
		<header class="pt-20 pb-10 text-center">
			<p class="text-xs tracking-[0.25em] uppercase text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mb-6">
				Project&nbsp;Note
			</p>
			<h1 class="font-display font-medium text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 leading-tight mb-4">
				EkNepal: A First Attempt at Building Around Uncertainty
			</h1>
		</header>

		<!-- ── Metadata ── -->
		<section class="pb-10">
			<dl class="grid grid-cols-[110px_1fr] gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm max-w-xl mx-auto">
				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Type</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Professional project</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Role</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Frontend contributor</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Organization</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Alpinist Studios</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Status</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Public product</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Source</dt>
				<dd class="text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">Proprietary — not published</dd>

				<dt class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 uppercase text-xs tracking-[0.1em] pt-0.5">Link</dt>
				<dd>
					<a href="https://eknepal.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-300 hover:text-accent-700 dark:hover:text-accent-200 transition-colors">
						eknepal.com&nbsp;↗
					</a>
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-t-4 border-double border-ink-900 dark:border-ink-100" />

		<!-- ── Abstract ── -->
		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="text-center text-sm tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 font-semibold mb-6">Abstract</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8] text-justify [hyphens:auto] max-w-2xl mx-auto">
				<p>
					EkNepal is a news-aggregation platform that brings reporting from multiple Nepali publications into a
					single interface. It was my first paid programming project. I contributed to the frontend while
					working through <strong class="font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Alpinist Studios</strong>.
					This note is a short retrospective on the product, my contribution to it, and what the experience
					changed about how I approach unclear problems.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<!-- ── 1. The Question ── -->
		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">1.</span>The Question
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p class="font-display text-xl italic text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">
					Could you get truthful information?
				</p>
				<p>
					Open a handful of Nepali news sites in a row and you get a handful of different accounts of the same
					country — the same event described differently, or reported by one outlet and missed entirely by the
					next. Nothing was necessarily wrong; there was just no single place that put the coverage side by
					side and let a reader compare it. That gap — not a bug, not a feature request, just a genuinely
					fuzzy problem — was the starting point for EkNepal.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<!-- ── 2. The Product ── -->
		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">2.</span>The Product
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p>
					EkNepal is a Nepali-language news reader that pulls reporting from several distinct outlets — among
					them Himalaya Times and News of Nepal — into one continuously updating feed, each item clearly
					attributed to its source publication. Articles carry share links (email, Facebook, X, Viber,
					WhatsApp) and a comment section, and the site is built mobile-first, with dates rendered in the
					Bikram Sambat calendar alongside a live weather readout. Beyond news, it bundles a set of everyday
					utilities Nepali readers commonly look for alongside their news — foreign-exchange rates, share-market
					figures, a horoscope, a date converter, a Unicode converter, and gold and silver pricing — organised
					behind a single navigation drawer.
				</p>
				<p>
					EkNepal is a product built and maintained by a team; it is not something I built alone, and I did not
					build its backend, its news-ingestion pipeline, or any fact-checking or source-classification system.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<!-- ── 3. My Contribution ── -->
		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">3.</span>My Contribution
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p>
					I contributed to the frontend of EkNepal through Alpinist Studios — the part that turned scattered
					reporting from multiple outlets into something a reader could actually navigate, read, and compare.
					It was my first paid software engineering work, and the first time code I wrote shipped to real
					users rather than a course instructor.
				</p>
			</div>
			{/*
				TODO (Atishaya): if you want more specifics than this (which components/pages you built,
				the exact stack, concrete technical decisions), send them and I'll expand this section.
				I didn't fabricate beyond what you've confirmed.
			*/}
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<!-- ── 4. Figures ── -->
		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-8">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">4.</span>Figures
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-10">
				<figure>
					<img
						src="/assets/eknepal/eknepal-fig-1-homepage.jpg"
						alt="EkNepal's primary news interface, showing a top-stories carousel and a feed of articles attributed to their source publications"
						width="1400"
						height="684"
						loading="lazy"
						class="w-full h-auto border border-rule dark:border-rule-dark"
					/>
					<figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 text-center">
						Figure 1: EkNepal's primary news interface
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<figure>
					<img
						src="/assets/eknepal/eknepal-fig-2-categories.jpg"
						alt="EkNepal's category navigation drawer, listing news, foreign exchange, share market, horoscope, and other sections"
						width="1400"
						height="680"
						loading="lazy"
						class="w-full h-auto border border-rule dark:border-rule-dark"
					/>
					<figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 text-center">
						Figure 2: Browsing reporting across categories
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<figure>
					<img
						src="/assets/eknepal/eknepal-fig-3-article.jpg"
						alt="An EkNepal article page, showing the source publication, share icons, and article body"
						width="1400"
						height="684"
						loading="lazy"
						class="w-full h-auto border border-rule dark:border-rule-dark"
					/>
					<figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 text-center">
						Figure 3: Article presentation
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<figure class="max-w-sm mx-auto">
					<img
						src="/assets/eknepal/eknepal-fig-4-responsiveness.jpg"
						alt="EkNepal's mobile-width layout, showing a single-column feed of video and article cards"
						width="724"
						height="1400"
						loading="lazy"
						class="w-full h-auto border border-rule dark:border-rule-dark"
					/>
					<figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 text-center">
						Figure 4: Responsive interface
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-rule dark:border-rule-dark" />

		<!-- ── 5. Reflection ── -->
		<section class="py-12">
			<h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 mb-6">
				<span class="text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-300 mr-2">5.</span>Reflection
			</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-[1.8]">
				<p>
					The habit EkNepal left me with wasn't a framework or a library — it was a way of starting: begin with
					a question that doesn't have a clean shape yet, break it into pieces small enough to actually build,
					ship something testable, and see what survives contact with real use. That's the same loop I now run
					on algorithms and proofs — state the conjecture, try small cases, build the smallest thing that could
					be wrong, and let the evidence tell you where the structure actually is.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<hr class="border-t-4 border-double border-ink-900 dark:border-ink-100" />

		<p class="py-12 text-center font-display text-xl italic text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100 max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
			If truth rarely arrives in one piece, why do we keep accepting it from a single source?
		</p>

		<p class="pb-16 text-center text-sm">
			<a href="/posts/eknepal-retrospective/" class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-300 hover:text-accent-700 dark:hover:text-accent-200 transition-colors">
				Read the personal retrospective →
			</a>
		</p>

	</article>
</Layout>
